---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { mailto, OPERATOR } from '../data/site';
---

<Prose
  title="Security"
  description="How NiftyFix keeps your files safe: every tool runs in an isolated, sandboxed frame that cannot upload them, and every input is validated."
  path="/security/"
>
  <h2>Isolation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every tool runs on a separate registrable domain, inside a sandboxed frame.</li>
    <li>
      The frame's Content Security Policy only allows loading its own static files and connecting to
      its own origin; form submissions, nested frames, plugins and base-URL changes are blocked.
    </li>
    <li>
      The page around the tool can receive only two kinds of message from it: the frame's height and
      coarse events such as "tool started". Messages are validated against a fixed schema that has
      no field able to carry file data.
    </li>
    <li>
      Processing happens in Web Workers. A crashed, cancelled or stalled worker is terminated and
      replaced, so one file cannot affect another.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Input validation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>File types are identified from their content signature, never from the file name alone.</li>
    <li>
      Image dimensions are read from the file header before decoding, and oversized images are
      rejected to prevent memory exhaustion.
    </li>
    <li>File size limits depend on the device class, and every job has a time limit.</li>
    <li>
      Settings are validated against a schema inside the worker, so tampered settings are rejected.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Reporting a vulnerability</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={mailto('Security report')}>{OPERATOR.email}</a> with the subject "Security
    report". Please give us a reasonable time to fix the issue before sharing it publicly.
  </p>
</Prose>
